Description: update_signal_state: keep a pending attribute-list save
 SharedData::add() and remove() ask the subscribe thread to save the attribute
 list (Action::UPDATE_PROP); update_signal_state() then set Action::SUBSCRIBE
 unconditionally. The action is one variable, so an AttributeStart right after
 an AttributeAdd (what the ConfigurationManager's AttributeAdd does) usually
 replaced the save before the thread saw it: the attribute was archived until
 the next restart, then gone from AttributeList. A burst of three adds through
 the ConfigurationManager saved none of them (0 of 3 after a restart); with this
 patch all three are saved and loaded again. UPDATE_PROP's handler goes on to
 SUBSCRIBE by itself, so leaving it in place loses nothing.
Author: Falak Sher <45312905+falaksherpk@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-10-24
---
--- a/src/SubscribeThread.cpp
+++ b/src/SubscribeThread.cpp
@@ -247,7 +247,17 @@
         break;
     }
     }
-    set_action(Action::SUBSCRIBE);
+    // A pending UPDATE_PROP (from add or remove) must not be overwritten: its handler
+    // saves the attribute list and then goes on to SUBSCRIBE anyway. Overwriting it lost
+    // the save of an attribute added and started in quick succession.
+    {
+        std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lk(action_mutex);
+        if(action != Action::UPDATE_PROP)
+        {
+            action = Action::SUBSCRIBE;
+        }
+    }
+    action_cv.notify_one();
 }
 
 //=============================================================================
